            <ArticleTitle>Clinical inquiry: is red-yeast rice a safe and effective alternative to statins?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>128-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with known coronary artery disease and dyslipidemia (secondary prevention), therapy with red-yeast rice extract containing naturally-occurring lovastatin is associated with a 30% reduction in coronary heart disease (CHD) mortality and a 60% reduction in myocardial infarction (MI), similar to the effect of statin medications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
